# EasyConfig

EasyConfig provides small, predictable configuration management for Python applications.

## Example

```python
from easyconfig import Config

config = Config(
    {"app": {"name": "demo"}, "debug": False},
    env_prefix="APP_",
)

print(config.get("app.name"))
print(config.require("debug"))
```

Environment variables override earlier sources. Double underscores represent nested keys:

```text
APP_DEBUG=true
APP_DATABASE__HOST=db.example.com
```

JSON and TOML files can be loaded with `Config.from_file("settings.toml", env_prefix="APP_")`.
